{
  "topic": "Animals with real superpowers",
  "language": "en",
  "format": "long",
  "category": "ciencia",
  "title": "ANIMALS with Real SUPERPOWERS 🐙🐦🐱",
  "hook": "Forget movie superheroes: there are animals with real powers that seem straight out of science fiction.",
  "presenter": "perro",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "role": "hook",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pul_hook",
      "narration": "Forget movie superheroes: there are animals with real powers that seem straight out of science fiction.",
      "on_screen_text": "Real superpowers",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Real"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "col_hook",
      "narration": "Three hearts, wings too fast to see, perfect landings and fly-proof stripes.",
      "on_screen_text": "Four incredible powers",
      "highlight_words": [
        "incredible"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "gato_hook",
      "narration": "I'm Leo, and although I'm a dog, today I'll introduce you to the superheroes of the animal kingdom.",
      "on_screen_text": "Animal superheroes",
      "highlight_words": [
        "superheroes"
      ],
      "sfx": "pop",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pul_hearts",
      "narration": "The octopus has three hearts: two pump blood to the gills and one to the rest of the body.",
      "on_screen_text": "Three hearts",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Three"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "The octopus"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pul_blue",
      "narration": "And its blood is blue, because it uses copper instead of iron to carry oxygen.",
      "on_screen_text": "Blue blood",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Blue"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pul_brain",
      "narration": "Two thirds of its neurons are in its arms. Each arm can explore almost on its own.",
      "on_screen_text": "Thinking arms",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Thinking"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pul_camo",
      "narration": "It can also change color and texture in an instant to hide.",
      "on_screen_text": "Instant camouflage",
      "highlight_words": [
        "camouflage"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "col_beats",
      "narration": "The hummingbird beats its wings up to about eighty times a second. That's why it buzzes like an insect.",
      "on_screen_text": "80 beats a second",
      "highlight_words": [
        "80"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "The hummingbird"
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "col_hover",
      "narration": "It can hover in place and even fly backwards, something almost no other bird can do.",
      "on_screen_text": "It flies backwards",
      "highlight_words": [
        "backwards"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "col_heart",
      "narration": "Its heart can beat more than twelve hundred times a minute.",
      "on_screen_text": "1,200 beats a minute",
      "highlight_words": [
        "1,200"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "col_ecuador",
      "narration": "And Ecuador is one of its best homes: more than a hundred species have been recorded there.",
      "on_screen_text": "100+ species in Ecuador",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Ecuador"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s12",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "gato_upside",
      "narration": "The cat has a famous trick: if it falls upside down, it almost always lands on its feet.",
      "on_screen_text": "Always on its feet",
      "highlight_words": [
        "feet"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "The cat"
    },
    {
      "id": "s13",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "gato_front",
      "narration": "First it twists the front half of its body, then the back half, without pushing off anything.",
      "on_screen_text": "It turns in halves",
      "highlight_words": [
        "halves"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s14",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "gato_kitten",
      "narration": "This reflex appears when they're kittens just three or four weeks old.",
      "on_screen_text": "From 3 weeks old",
      "highlight_words": [
        "3"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s15",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ceb_hook",
      "narration": "And zebra stripes? They're not just for looks: they work as a fly repellent.",
      "on_screen_text": "Fly-proof stripes",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Fly-proof"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "The zebra"
    },
    {
      "id": "s16",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ceb_miss",
      "narration": "Biting flies get confused by the stripes, brake badly and barely manage to land.",
      "on_screen_text": "Flies miss",
      "highlight_words": [
        "miss"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s17",
      "role": "surprise",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ceb_experiment",
      "narration": "Surprise: in an experiment, horses wearing striped coats got far fewer fly landings.",
      "on_screen_text": "Horses in zebra pajamas!",
      "highlight_words": [
        "zebra"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s18",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pez_gills",
      "narration": "And fish breathe underwater, where there's far less oxygen than in air.",
      "on_screen_text": "Breathing underwater",
      "highlight_words": [
        "underwater"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "The fish"
    },
    {
      "id": "s19",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pez_counter",
      "narration": "Their gills use a countercurrent trick that lets them pull out up to eighty percent of the oxygen.",
      "on_screen_text": "Up to 80% of the oxygen",
      "highlight_words": [
        "80"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s20",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pez_shark",
      "narration": "Some sharks even have to keep swimming so water flows over their gills.",
      "on_screen_text": "Swim to breathe",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Swim"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s21",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "abe_shapes",
      "narration": "And bees build hexagons, the shape that stores the most honey with the least wax.",
      "on_screen_text": "Hexagon engineers",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Hexagon"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pul_swim",
      "narration": "And when it swims, the heart that feeds its body stops. That's why it prefers to crawl along the bottom.",
      "on_screen_text": "It prefers to crawl",
      "highlight_words": [
        "crawl"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s23",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pul_squeeze",
      "narration": "Since it has no bones, it can squeeze through any hole bigger than its beak.",
      "on_screen_text": "No bones",
      "highlight_words": [
        "bones"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s24",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pul_taste",
      "narration": "And its suckers can taste what they touch. It's like having tongues on your fingers.",
      "on_screen_text": "Suckers that taste",
      "highlight_words": [
        "taste"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s25",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "col_lift",
      "narration": "Its wings trace a figure eight in the air, pushing both on the way down and on the way up.",
      "on_screen_text": "Figure-eight wings",
      "highlight_words": [
        "eight"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s26",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "col_torpor",
      "narration": "At night it goes into torpor: it lowers its temperature and heart rate to save energy until dawn.",
      "on_screen_text": "Night-time power saving",
      "highlight_words": [
        "saving"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "gato_ear",
      "narration": "Its inner ear tells it in a split second where the ground is.",
      "on_screen_text": "The inner ear",
      "highlight_words": [
        "ear"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "gato_photo",
      "narration": "Scientists studied it back in 1894, with one of the first photo sequences in history.",
      "on_screen_text": "Photos from 1894",
      "highlight_words": [
        "1894"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s29",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ceb_unique",
      "narration": "And no two zebras have the same stripes: each one has its own pattern.",
      "on_screen_text": "Unique stripes",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Unique"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pez_lamellae",
      "narration": "Gills have thousands of very thin plates, giving a huge surface to catch oxygen.",
      "on_screen_text": "Super-thin plates",
      "highlight_words": [
        "plates"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s31",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pul_ink",
      "narration": "If it's attacked, it squirts a cloud of ink and escapes while the enemy is confused.",
      "on_screen_text": "A cloud of ink",
      "highlight_words": [
        "ink"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s32",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "col_eight",
      "narration": "It weighs less than a small coin, yet some can migrate long distances.",
      "on_screen_text": "Small but well-traveled",
      "highlight_words": [
        "traveled"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s33",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "gato_tuck",
      "narration": "It tucks and stretches its legs to spin faster or slower, like a figure skater.",
      "on_screen_text": "Like a figure skater",
      "highlight_words": [
        "skater"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s34",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "gato_land",
      "narration": "Finally it lands with its legs as shock absorbers. Even so, high falls can still hurt it.",
      "on_screen_text": "Shock-absorbing legs",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Shock-absorbing"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ceb_skin",
      "narration": "Under its black and white coat, a zebra's skin is dark.",
      "on_screen_text": "Dark skin underneath",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Dark"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s36",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pez_oxygen",
      "narration": "Water holds twenty to forty times less oxygen than air. Breathing there is a huge challenge.",
      "on_screen_text": "Little oxygen in water",
      "highlight_words": [
        "oxygen"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s37",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "abe_less",
      "narration": "Bees need several kilos of honey to make one kilo of wax, so they can't afford to waste it.",
      "on_screen_text": "Wax is precious",
      "highlight_words": [
        "precious"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s38",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "col_hook",
      "narration": "Nature has been inventing superpowers for millions of years. You just have to know where to look.",
      "on_screen_text": "Millions of years of invention",
      "highlight_words": [
        "invention"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s39",
      "role": "closing",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pul_outro",
      "narration": "What's your favorite animal? Tell me in the comments and it might be next.",
      "on_screen_text": "What's your favorite?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "favorite?"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    }
